        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "って (a contracted form of と) is a casual quoting particle used to mark direct or indirect speech, thoughts, feelings, or to introduce a topic casually. For example, 行くって言っていた means '[They] were saying [they] will go.' といってもいい combines と with 言う and いい, meaning 'You/one could say' (literally: 'It's fine even if one says...').",
